@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Context
+
+`createTask` trims and builds a task without checks; `list.ts` calls it, `renameTask` and `addTag` return plain tasks. No `TodoErrorCode` fits bad input.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** reject the four kinds of invalid input in `add`, `rename`, `tag`, with clear messages; leave the list untouched on rejection.
+**Non-Goals:** validating lookups (`find`, `untag`, `remove`), filters, or existing tasks.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add error code `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode` (none of the existing codes fit).
+- Put pure validators in `task.ts` (`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`), each returning `Result` of the cleaned value; no throwing.
+- `createTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` return `Result<Task>` and use the validators; `list.ts` checks `if (!result.ok) return result;`.
+- In `add`, validation runs before the duplicate check and the id counter is incremented only after success, so a rejection consumes no id. In `rename`, validate the new title before the duplicate check.
+- Length is measured on the trimmed title, in JavaScript string length (UTF-16 units).
+- The priority is validated at runtime since screens pass untyped input.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Changing `createTask`/`renameTask`/`addTag` to return `Result` breaks internal callers and tests that use them directly; they are updated in this change. They are not exported from `src/index.ts`.
