@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank titles, huge titles, unknown priorities, tags with spaces. The list should refuse them with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject invalid input with a new error code `invalid-input` and a message saying what is wrong:
+  - a title that is empty or only spaces;
+  - a title longer than 120 characters (after trimming);
+  - a priority other than `low`, `normal`, `high`;
+  - a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- When input is rejected, the list is unchanged (no task added, renamed or tagged, and no id consumed).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: validation of titles, priorities and tags when a task is added, renamed or tagged.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Project rules touched: "Errors are returned as a Result in the domain" (validation returns `Result`, never throws); "TSDoc on every exported function" (new validators are documented); "No wall clock or randomness" and "no new runtime dependency" are untouched. `createTask` becomes fallible (returns `Result<Task>`), as the conventions say pure task logic returns `Result` where it can fail.
+- Public API in `src/index.ts`: the `TodoErrorCode` type gains `'invalid-input'`. No new exported functions; `add`, `rename` and `tag` already return `Result`.
+- Code: `src/domain/result.ts`, `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `test/`.
